  "material_learning": "Treasury inversion is a real macroeconomic state but not a usable lagged BTC allocation rule in this sample. The primary 10Y-minus-3M definition captured a strong Design period yet reduced drawdown only from 77.18955925 to 74.05097969 percent, short of the frozen fifteen-percent relative reduction. During 2023-2024 it stayed almost entirely in cash, had only 2.46238030 percent average exposure, entered once, returned -7.86218115 percent while passive BTC returned 464.75475156 percent, and terminal liquidation worsened the result. The 10Y-minus-1Y and 10Y-minus-2Y neighbors retained only 1.658232 and 13.212236 percent of passive Validation upside and both failed their Calmar gates. The apparent Design success is period concentration, not stable alpha.",
